  "divergence": {
    "id": "A22",
    "report": "A22",
    "note": "The baseline assigns provenance inside the substitution loop, so only the LAST placeholder survives: the entry says the value came from variable B and records nothing about A, which came from an explicit host override. SPEC.md 6 requires provenance to say which layer supplied a value, and the answer here is two layers. The Dart implementation records every contributing variable and the highest-precedence source among them, keeping the single-variable shape byte-identical to the baseline."
  },
